    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">WHY BICARB?</p>
    <h2>The same bicarbonate ion has real performance research behind it.</h2>
    <p>Bicarbonate is a <strong>key part of the body’s normal buffering system</strong>. In a 2026 randomized crossover trial, trained cyclists co-ingesting bicarbonate + carbohydrate during a 3-hour ride produced <strong>12 W more</strong> in a subsequent 12-minute time trial. In a 2024 randomized trial, <strong>0.3 g/kg sodium bicarbonate</strong> cut about <strong>54 seconds</strong> from a 40-km cycling time trial.</p>
    <p><strong>Different doses. Same ion. Bicarb Bonus™ hydration, without the megadose.</strong></p>
    <p><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/42788859/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">2026 cycling trial</a> · <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39068627/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">2024 40-km trial</a></p>
